        "text": "On October 18, 2017, FBI officers mistakenly raided 3756 Denville Trace, a family home occupied by petitioners Hilliard Toi Cliatt, Curtrina\u202fMartin, and her seven\u2011year\u2011old son."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners filed a claim under the Federal Tort Claims Act alleging negligent and intentional actions by the officers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch asked whether homeowners may sue the government for damages when federal officers raid the wrong house."
      }
    ],
